      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not take any insulin while you are feeling this shaky and dizzy; this indicates your blood sugar is still dangerously low. Taking insulin could cause another severe low blood sugar episode, which can be very dangerous. If simple carbs didn't help, try rubbing a small amount of glucose gel on your gums or sipping a sugary sports drink, and continue to monitor yourself closely. If the symptoms persist or worsen, calling a telehealth line or urgent care might be a safer and less expensive next step than waiting.",
