      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is critical that you do not try to manage this severe feeling of instability with insulin right now, as your body needs blood sugar to come up first. Taking even a small dose of insulin when you are hypoglycemic will further drop your blood sugar, making you much sicker. Please call your doctor's on-call line or a local nurse advice line for immediate guidance tailored to your specific situation. They can advise you on the safest next steps while you are waiting for the higher blood sugar to stabilize naturally.",
